{"claims":[{"claim_text":"A capitalist society will not be reformed into a socialist one, just as capitalism itself was not born through welcomed reforms to the former feudal order.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"Popular legislation and politicians with benevolent intentions can help create more favorable conditions for change, but these things alone cannot bring the revolutionary overhaul we seek: a complete upheaval of the present economic system that extracts value from the many for the private profit of the few.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion","evaluation"],"evidence_ids":[1]},{"claim_text":"DSA can support a Revolutionary movement.", "claim_types":["policy_position"],"evidence_ids":[3]},{"claim_text":"Revolutionary situations are generated primarily by the intersection of two factors: by a sustained crisis in the system, and an organization (or organizations) being capable of exploiting that crisis.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"Crises are continually generated by any inept governance that attempts to suppress class conflict and prop up an unsustainable capitalism or hegemony by force, and include economic crisis, climate change, and war.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"In 2020 alone, there was a triple crisis of a pandemic, a collapse in employment, and a nationwide uprising against police violence.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[4]},{"claim_text":"Even in the acute moment of crisis in 2020, there was not a revolutionary situation.", "claim_types":["factual_assertion"],"evidence_ids":[4]}],"unresolved_references":[]}
